title: <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**DNVP**</span> Leadership Vote
subtitle: Hugenberg has angered his party.
view-if: dnvp_leader = "Hugenberg" and year = 1929 and month = 11 and dnvp_congress_1929_seen == 0
on-arrival: dnvp_congress_1929_seen = 1
max-visits: 1
tags: event
face-image: img/portraits/KVP_logo.jpg
new-page: true

= <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**DNVP**</span> Congress

Factions withitn the <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**DNVP**</span> have clashed with one another increasingly often under Hugenberg's leadership. His attemps to assert control over the party and the fallout from the Young Plan have made a party split virtually inevitable.

- @resultsdnvp: The congress unfolds...

@resultsdnvp
go-to: treviranus if pro_republic >= 75; hugenberg if pro_republic < 75

@treviranus
on-arrival: dnvp_leader = "Treviranus"; dnvp_ideology = "National Conservatism"; dnvp_left = 1; dnvp_color = "#3F7BC1"; dvp_left -= 1
face-image: img/portraits/TreviranusGottfried.jpg
go-to: dnf_formed

Hugenberg's all-or-nothing strategy and the decline in support for the <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">*var(--dnvp-color)**</span> have convinced the party to oust him. Replacing Hugenberg is Gottfried Treviranus, a member of the Young Conservatives, in favor of constructive participation within the Republic. As a response, Hugenberg has threatened to leave the party and form his own.

@hugenberg
on-arrival: pro_republic -= 5; dnvp_ideology = "Authoritarian Conservatism"; dnvp_color = "#003755"; dnvp_left = -2; dvp_left += 1
face-image: img/portraits/HugenbergAlfred.jpg
go-to: kvp_formed

Hugenberg has managed to consolidate power within his party, even the combined votes of moderates and agrarians were unable to oust him. The anti-Hugenberg forces have scattered all over the political right, with committed nationalist forming the <span style="color: #455B95;">**Konservative Volkspartei**</span>.
